* Measure tt_um_lelo_temp_wulffern: does it start, and at what frequency
.control
echo "MEAS_START"

set fend = .raw
foreach vtemp -40 25 125

load {cicname}_$vtemp$fend

*- the oscillator through the wrapper: period between rising edges
meas tran t1_$vtemp WHEN v(uo_out[0])=0.9 RISE=1 FROM={t_start}
meas tran t2_$vtemp WHEN v(uo_out[0])=0.9 RISE=5 FROM={t_start}
*- no `let freq_` here: a negative temperature makes t1_-40 parse
*- as subtraction. t1/t2 land in the results; frequency is 4/(t2-t1)
*- in post-processing.
*- the tie-low resistors hold every uio as an input
meas tran oe0_$vtemp FIND v(uio_oe[0]) AT={t_stop}
meas tran oe7_$vtemp FIND v(uio_oe[7]) AT={t_stop}

*- supply current, running and powered down
meas tran idd_$vtemp AVG i(vdd) from={t_start} to={t_stop}
meas tran iddq_$vtemp AVG i(vdd) from=0.5u to=1.5u

end
echo "MEAS_END"
.endc
